      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Originally called Yellow Banks for the color of its Ohio River bluffs, Owensboro was renamed in 1893 to its current spelling.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owensboro%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1884, the Owensboro Wagon Company became one of the nation’s largest wagon manufacturers, shaping regional transport.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
